[h1]RICE Unofficial Update[/h1]

[b]This is an unofficial update of RICE, made with the author's permission. It is not made or supported by @cybrxkhan.[/b] It will be retired as soon as RICE gets an official update for CK3 1.21.

[h2]What is RICE?[/h2]

[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2273832430]Regional Immersion and Cultural Enrichment (RICE)[/url] by cybrxkhan is a collection of "flavor packs" that add immersion to different regions, cultures, and religions in CK3, with a focus on lesser-known places, peoples, and histories. Please visit the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2273832430]original mod page[/url] for its full description, credits, and links, and rate and favorite the original mod if you enjoy it.

[h2]What does this update do?[/h2]

The original RICE on Steam is for CK3 1.19. This update adapts it to 1.20 and 1.21, through pull requests to RICE on GitHub (the 1.20 one is merged).

[h3]CK3 1.20[/h3]

CK3 1.20 changed how religions work: many former faiths became rites of a broader faith, and doctrines and tenets now belong to rites. This part takes the 1.20 beta version of RICE and finishes its adaptation:

[list]
[*] Religions, faiths, and rites restructured for 1.20, and all faith references in decisions, events, history, and bookmarks updated to the new faiths and rites.
[*] Fixed a crash on loading, caused by decisions with two widgets.
[*] Fixed load errors caused by other 1.20 changes.
[*] Restored the Greenland and Sri Lanka struggle legend seeds, which were disabled in the beta.
[*] Fixed faith conversions at game start and in events and decisions, which failed under the new 1.20 conversion rules.
[*] Fixed RICE's landless adventurers not being playable, a known issue of the beta.
[*] Fixed Christian faiths before and after the Great Schism, e.g. Christians being interlopers in the Normandy and Sicily struggles, and Icelandic rulers not converting to Insular.
[*] Fixed decisions with option lists skipping their options and going straight to confirmation.
[*] Fixed the Nile River situation ending after its first year.
[*] Fixed a number of bugs found while testing.
[/list]

The full list of changes is in the [url=https://github.com/cybrxkhan/RICE-for-CK3/pull/345]1.20 pull request on GitHub[/url].

[h3]CK3 1.21[/h3]

CK3 1.21 replaced special and duchy buildings with districts, renamed development to prosperity, reworked control, taxes, and the economy, added merchants, and changed parts of the map and history:

[list]
[*] Special and duchy buildings converted to districts, the way vanilla converted its own.
[*] Renamed and removed modifiers converted the way vanilla converted its own, e.g. each tax bonus now applies to one type of tax.
[*] New vanilla conventions followed, e.g. control values for men-at-arms, title types for adventurer camps, and AI values for duchy districts.
[*] The new counties of Sicily and Apulia (Trapani, Catania, Caltagirone, Taranto) get the RICE setups of the counties they came from, the Sawdan aspiration's "Control Rome" objective uses the new county of Rome, and RICE's regions include the new duchies.
[*] Start setups adjusted to the new history, e.g. Cao Yijin now starts as Count of Liaoquan in 867.
[*] Characters that vanilla added in 1.21 replace RICE's own versions: the Najahids, Li Mingzhen's family, Pei Xiu, and the merchants Wuhsha al-Dallala, Hugo von Hildesheim, and Guglielmo Grasso.
[*] RICE's wars use the new 1.21 war end effects, and its border raids destroy buildings, as vanilla's do since 1.21. The Norman adventure grants fewer troops, as vanilla's Varangian adventure does since 1.21.
[*] The Luxor temple, church, and mosque are separate districts now, switched by the "Rededicate Luxor Temple" decision.
[*] Restored the holy sites that vanilla removed in 1.20, which some RICE faiths still had.
[*] Fixed issues found while testing, some of which already existed in RICE 1.20, e.g. rites and tenets missed in 1.20, Nubia's prosperity applied twice, and Tarim adventurers losing their camps.
[/list]

The full list of changes is in the [url=https://github.com/cybrxkhan/RICE-for-CK3/pull/349]1.21 pull request on GitHub[/url].

[h2]Open questions[/h2]

Some changes needed decisions only the author can make. In each case, this update makes the choice that seemed the most logical one, e.g.:

[list]
[*] [b]Yazidi, Yarsani, and Kurdish pagan[/b] are rites of the Yazidi faith, with one head of faith.
[*] [b]Nile River forecasts[/b] always come true, as the 1.20 engine ends the situation when the next flood is picked at random.
[*] [b]Unfinished beta content[/b] (e.g. the Sammitiya Buddhists in Sindh) is skipped until the missing characters are added.
[*] [b]Taxes:[/b] each RICE tax bonus applies to the type of tax that fits its theme, e.g. religious tax for temples and commerce tax for trade.
[*] [b]Icelandic culture:[/b] RICE's own definition replaces vanilla's new one, with vanilla's new Icelandic name list.
[*] [b]Luxor:[/b] each switch between the temple, church, and mosque costs major prestige, plus the 1000 gold and 1000 piety that building one of them costs.
[/list]

The full lists are in the pull requests linked above.

[h2]Known limitations[/h2]

[list]
[*] [b]Duchy districts at game start:[/b] 1.21 can't create duchy districts by script, so the Tiraz factories (Ahvaz, Cordoba, Cairo), the Breton free range (Vannes), and the Socotra dragon blood forest are no longer placed at game start. They can still be built.
[/list]

[h2]Is it playable?[/h2]

Yes. The update was tested by:

[list]
[*] Static analysis with [url=https://github.com/amtep/tiger]ck3-tiger[/url], compared with the previous RICE version.
[*] Starting all three bookmarks (867, 1066, 1178) and checking the error log.
[*] Running the game in observer mode for 30+ years.
[*] Manual testing of the areas affected by both updates.
[/list]

That said, RICE is a large mod and not everything could be tested. [b]Most issues that already existed in RICE 1.19 are not addressed by this update.[/b] Those found while testing are reported on GitHub. Translations for content new in the beta are still missing in languages other than English.

The beta also contained the unfinished [b]"Jats and Sammitiya"[/b] flavor pack, with new Buddhist schools such as Sarvastivada, Pudgalavada, Dharmaguptaka, and Mahasanghika. It is included as is, so issues there are to be expected.

[h2]Save compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*] [b]Not compatible with existing saves.[/b] Start a new game.
[*] Saves made with this update [b]may not be compatible[/b] with future official RICE versions.
[/list]

[h2]Usage[/h2]

[list]
[*] Use this mod [b]instead of[/b] the original RICE, never both. Disable the original RICE in your playset.
[*] Load it in the same place as the original RICE.
[*] Only RICE itself is updated. RICE works with EPE without any compatibility patch. The only difference is that RICE's own cultures use RICE appearances instead of EPE's. The existing RICE + EPE patch still works on 1.20 if you want EPE appearances for them, but it's outdated and undoes some minor RICE changes (traditions for a few cultures, some coats of arms and bookmark portraits).
[/list]

[h2]Reporting issues[/h2]

Please report issues in the comments, but [b]only if they appear to be related to this update[/b], e.g. religions, faiths, rites, and doctrines (1.20), buildings, districts, and the economy (1.21), or anything that worked in RICE 1.19 and no longer does. Include the game date, your character, and any related lines from [i]error.log[/i] if possible. Issues that also existed in RICE 1.19 should go to the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2273832430]original mod[/url].
